{"created": "2026-07-07T10:16:07.299642+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-04T06:58:14.286810+00:00", "id": 21236659, "conceptrecid": "20694687", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20694687", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "metadata": {"title": "Probe traces for \"Edge-Inference Governors Need Memory-Clock State\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "publication_date": "2026-07-07", "description": "<p>Bulk raw measurement traces underlying the paper \"Edge-Inference Governors<br>Need Memory-Clock State\" (Jaehoon Kang), arXiv:2606.16106.</p>\n<p>This archive holds the large raw traces kept out of the companion code<br>repository for size reasons. The measurement harness, campaign runners,<br>analysis scripts, per-run summaries, and the deployed-governor result tables<br>live at https://github.com/dankang21/jetson-latency-lab &mdash; this dataset<br>complements the repository with bulk per-cycle and per-transition traces<br>only. SHA256SUMS is included for integrity verification.</p>\n<p>Contents of this version<br>- partb_ext_nano.tar.gz &mdash; Part-B extension: 100,000-cycle tail cells on the<br>&nbsp; Orin Nano (ViT-Small and L2-resident GEMM x EMC x adversary).<br>- partb_nx.tar.gz &mdash; Orin NX Part-B burst-replication matrix (EMC 2133/3199<br>&nbsp; MHz x adversary) plus worst-cell repeats (nx_pb_*).<br>- e4_replication_nano.tar.gz &mdash; Orin Nano root-protocol replication runs<br>&nbsp; (nano_rep_*) for the independent burst replication.<br>- e3_governor_nx.tar.gz &mdash; auxiliary clock-lock/readback traces for the<br>&nbsp; Orin NX deployed-governor cells.<br>- soak_power_1khz.csv.gz &mdash; INA3221 VDD_IN power trace of the one-hour saturated&nbsp;Qwen2.5 decode soak, sampled as fast as the driver allows (median interval 3.6 ms; the \"1khz\" in the file name is a misnomer).<br>- nx_probe_emc_3199_2133.csv.gz, nx_probe_gpu_1173_816.csv.gz &mdash; Orin NX<br>&nbsp; EMC/GPU frequency-transition probe traces (per-quantum, cycle-counted).<br>- Carried over from the previous version: the Orin Nano per-pair<br>&nbsp; frequency-transition probe traces (*.probe.csv) for the EMC/CPU/GPU<br>&nbsp; actuation campaigns.</p>\n<p>Platforms: NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super (8 GB, L4T R36.5) and Jetson Orin<br>NX 16 GB (L4T R36.4.3), JetPack 6. Each run carries its locked CPU/GPU/EMC<br>clocks, power mode, and command line in a .meta.json or in-file header; CSV<br>column definitions are documented in the harness repository.</p>\n<p>This version adds the two-SKU deployed-governor and contract-admission era<br>datasets (tail-cell extension, NX burst replication, governor auxiliaries,<br>soak power trace, NX transition probes) to the earlier probe-trace release.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kang, Jaehoon", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0008-1020-9533"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "arXiv:2606.16106", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "arxiv"}], "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/dankang21/jetson-latency-lab"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "apache2.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20694687"}}]}}, "title": "Probe traces for \"Edge-Inference Governors Need Memory-Clock State\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21236659", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21236659", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21236659?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21236659", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21236659/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20694687", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20694687", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20694687", "parent_doi_h